						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, December 09, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Black Reavers & CoM! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							<html><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Last evening a few of us took a little journey to CoM. You know, that place that drops the JADE REAVER'S? Well, we ran the circuit of reavers. And then ventured down to start over. Only had one JR drop and need like a trillion more for needy Druids and Rangers in our guilds. (We had 5 out of 13 people rolling for JR's, each representing a different guild. Our one druid received his JR on the first circuit. GRATS Leaves!) We zip back down and in to the first room, clear out the trash and pull the last<BR>reaver.</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">As a side note: Dryzun and a some guildies of his at Darkblood compadres had come down to get Rak for the completion of his Spear of Fate Shammy Epic... Grats Dry!</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Anyway, we get the reaver and another spawns, and then another, and another... Those of you that have experienced this are shaking your heads going &quot;Uh huh... and at what reaver did you all bite it<BR>at or evac at?&quot;</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Bah, we thrive on death and destruction!</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Sometime after the 12th spawn I petitioned. Ok, call me chicken... but there was no way I was going to get popped for exploiting some bug.</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">As this was happening DB jumped in and aided in keeping our MA Sunnybeach, healed. Their Mages kept us supplied with rods and our chanter saw more work in that 1 hour than probably in the past few weeks! Yes, 1 hour.. I went through two full rounds of C2!</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Somewhere around the 30th spawn a Guide popped in. She left after watching for a few to get a GM. The GM came somewhere towards the end or after the spawning stopped finally. I am unsure, but I think we hit a new Kunark record for Reaver pops...<BR><b>87 A BLACK REAVERS DEAD!</b></font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">And NOT ONE DEATH suffered!</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">The GM never told us it was a bug as Sunny was<BR>talking to him, so we will assume..., ahh love that word ASSUME!, that it was NOT a bug. Just a heads up gang... It CAN be done and you CAN live through that eternal endless black reaver spawn!</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">My hat goes off to Darkblood members present and all our friends that gathered to get those bad boys. Oh and only 2 JR's dropped off those 87.. BAH HUMBUG!</font></p><BR><p><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Ecclesiastique has carpal tunnel now!</font></p><BR><p><a href="http://pub89.ezboard.com/fsacredhonorfrm5.showMessage?topicID=170.topic"><b><font face="Lucida Handwriting" size="2">Yesterday in CoM</font></b></a></p><BR><font size="2"><BR><BR><center><a href=mailto:Adrastea_Trailtracker@hotmail.com><b><font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting">Adrastea</font></b> <font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting"> Trailtracker</font></a><font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting">&nbsp;<img src="http://www.graphxkingdom.com/graphics/christmas/xmas004.gif" width="32" height="32"> </font> <a href=mailto:Adrastea_Trailtracker@hotmail.com><b><font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting">Ecclesiastique</font></b> <font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting"> Dehonneur</font></a><font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting">&nbsp;<img src="http://www.graphxkingdom.com/graphics/christmas/xmas004.gif" width="32" height="32"><a href=mailto:Adrastea_Trailtracker@hotmail.com><b></b></a></font><a href=mailto:Adrastea_Trailtracker@hotmail.com><b><font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting">Kuhrizmuh</font></b><font color="#FF0000" face="Lucida Handwriting"> Krystallyn</font></a></center></font><BR><center><font face="Lucida Handwriting" color="#FF0000"><BR><img src="http://www.thesitefights.com/team28b/Holiday/dec/logo.gif" width="340" height="204"></font><font face="Lucida Handwriting" color="#FF0000" size="2"><BR><BR></font><a href=http://eqsacredhonor.tripod.com/><b><font color="#009150" size="2" face="Lucida Handwriting">Sacred Honor Guild</font></b></a><font size="2"><font face="Lucida Handwriting" color="#FF0000"><b>&nbsp;</b><img src="http://www.graphxkingdom.com/graphics/christmas/xmas004.gif" width="32" height="32"><a href=http://members.tripod.com/seliastrailtracker/links1.html><b></b></a></font></font><b><a href=http://members.tripod.com/seliastrailtracker/links1.html><font color="#009150" size="2" face="Lucida Handwriting">Trailtracker Website</font></a></b><font size="2"><font face="Lucida Handwriting" color="#FF0000">&nbsp;<img src="http://www.graphxkingdom.com/graphics/christmas/xmas004.gif" width="32" height="32"><a href=http://www.solusekro.com/eq/guilds.asp><b></b></a></font></font><b><a href=http://www.solusekro.com/eq/guilds.asp><font color="#009150" size="2" face="Lucida Handwriting">Solusek Ro</font></a></b><font color="#FF0000" size="3"><BR></font></center></html><BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=343">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Sunday, December 08, 2002</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Website update. </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Website of the "Avalanche of Power" guild is now part of the "Lords of Prophecy" guild website. <BR><BR>All AoP members have always had open invite to all non-level restricted events of Lords and share same raid channel with us. As a natural evolution we merged our websites as well.<BR><BR>Begining of the year 2003 we expect to merge both guild under Lords flag. <BR><BR>For more information please visit us at:<BR><BR>http://www.geocities.com/enigmesolro<BR><BR>Thank you,<BR><BR>Flaor McLife,<BR>"da white bear"<BR>Leader of the "Lords of Prophecy" <BR><BR>Jykocco, <BR>Leader of the "Avalanche of Power"
							<br><BR>
							 - Flaor<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=342">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Tuesday, December 03, 2002</p></TD></TR>
